module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.admission_roster_read_as_the_whole_membership_rule

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data admission_roster_read_as_the_whole_membership_rule: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "admission_roster_read_as_the_whole_membership_rule" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an admission roster is read as the whole membership rule** (INVALID STATE: a hand-authored roster states a NECESSARY condition for a subject to be selected, a reader verifies the subject against that roster, and the roster's answer is then treated as the SUFFICIENT and only answer -- while the selecting mechanism carries additional admission paths the roster does not mention, and a completed run has already published which subjects it actually selected. ",

    "HARM: the reader concludes a thing does not execute, and acts on it. That is worse than an ordinary wrong belief, because the actions it licenses are removals -- an enrolment withdrawn, a probe left unrouted, evidence declared dormant -- each justified by the non-execution and each invisible afterwards, since a subject believed not to run produces nothing whose absence anyone notices. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, AND IT IS WHAT SEPARATES THIS FROM REASONING BADLY: THE ANSWER WAS PUBLISHED AND FREE. The mechanism's own run emits a per-subject disposition receipt, so membership is a fact to be READ, not derived. The roster was consulted because it is the artifact a reader can hold in mind; the receipt was skipped because holding it requires downloading it. That is a convenience gradient, not a knowledge gap, which is why verifying harder against the roster cannot fix it. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, AND BOTH PARTIES MADE IT INDEPENDENTLY ON THE SAME RUN, gunbc 2026-09-07 (#10783).** test.claim.argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test matches no prefix in v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes. From that, an author concluded the required floor discovers and does not run it, described the module as dormant in two carrier rows, and REMOVED its two expecting-red identities from v2.workflow.floor_expected_red on the ground that enrolling a never-executed identity asserts something false. A reviewer reached the same conclusion from the same roster, and a manager verified the prefix list and stopped there. The floor also plans a witness whose FILE THE CHANGE TOUCHES. The same run's required-floor-disposition artifact carries all four of that module's identities at disposition planned_as_changed_witness, with the two expecting-red arms recorded as held reds rather than as never-executed rows. That artifact is the instrument and it is named here rather than quoted: download required-floor-disposition from the run and read those identities by header name. An earlier cut of this receipt transcribed the census denominator, which is a run-local number nothing re-derives -- the same defect, in the row filed to catch reading errors. Un-enrolled, those two arms block their own landing change, which is the change that necessarily runs them. ",

    "THE INSTRUMENT, NAMED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED (DESIGN section 6): required-floor-disposition, published as an artifact by every completed run of gunbc.witness_floor_workflow, one row per discovered identity carrying its disposition and outcome. Re-derive with gh run download <run id> -R <repo> -n required-floor-disposition and group by the disposition column read BY HEADER NAME. Its sibling required-floor-claim-cost answers cost on the same population and by the same route. ",

    "WHAT SEPARATES THIS FROM ITS THREE NEAREST NEIGHBOURS, stated because folding it into any of them would lose the actionable part. roster_is_its_own_denominator is a roster that is SHORT -- it should hold a row and does not, so the receipt over it is incomplete; this roster is CORRECT and complete for what it governs, and the defect is reading it as governing more than it does. absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked is an instrument answering over a region it never read; here the instrument read its region correctly and the reader asked it a question it does not answer. selection_view_read_as_population is a threshold over MEASURED values mistaken for the population; this roster carries no measurement at all. The shared consequence is a confident claim about a population, and the shared remedy is not shared: only this one is fixed by reading a receipt that already exists. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The defect is caught by a reviewer, or by the run refusing, after the removal it licensed has been authored. **CEILING: 1, AND THE REASON IS DECIDABILITY RATHER THAN UNBUILT WORK.** The invalid state is a belief a reader forms about what a mechanism selects. Nothing in the corpus is malformed at the moment it forms -- the roster is correct, the code is well-formed, and the only artifact carrying the wrong conclusion is prose, which DESIGN section 4c puts out of reach of any fold. So there is no state to make unwritable and no evaluator to write, which is DESIGN section 5's ratchet-forever case; calling this mechanically preventable would name a mechanism that cannot exist and would let the row read as coverage it does not provide. An earlier revision of this row DID claim ceiling 2 while its trigger named only review diligence, which is rung 1 -- the grain mismatch DESIGN section 4b(3) names as its own review tell, committed here in the row filed to catch reading errors. ",

    "**NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none, and stating that honestly is the point.** This is a review-time recognition rule, and reading admission rosters more carefully does not retire it. What retires an INSTANCE is not a mechanism but a question asked before the conclusion is drawn -- has a completed run already published this, and what does its receipt say. ",

    "WHAT WOULD CHANGE THE ANALYSIS, stated as a conditional and deliberately NOT as a trigger. If a claim about whether a subject executes were carried as TYPED DATA rather than as prose, the join against a run's disposition receipt would be decidable and a fold could refuse a claim that disagrees with the receipt. That is available per fact and not as a mechanism: it removes one claim from this class's reach, exactly as moving an obligation into a typed carrier does elsewhere, and it leaves every claim still written as prose untouched. Writing it in the trigger field would produce a trigger satisfied by one row moving while the class stayed alive, which is the failure DESIGN section 4b(3) describes when a trigger names less than the capability it restores. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, AND IT IS ONE QUESTION: when about to claim that something does or does not run, ask whether a completed run has already published the answer, and read that instead. PREFER THE RUN'S OWN RECEIPT TO ANY ROSTER YOU CAN REASON FROM. The behavioural tell is a sentence of the form 'it matches no X, so it is not run' with no artifact cited beside it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
